# DACore Integration

DACore is an admin-UI **module**, not framework core — but its files are **as forbidden as `app/parts/`**. Full docs: `AIRULES/30-DACORE-OVERVIEW.md` … `36`.

**Why:** DACore is installed and updated as a package. Any edit, patch, or extra file under `app/modules/DACore/` **disappears on the next DACore update**. You may only *use* what DACore already provides. New features belong in **your own** module.

## Never

- Edit, patch, delete, or **add** any file under `app/modules/DACore/` (no exceptions, even if the user asks)
- `INSERT`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE` on `dacore_menu`, `dacore_ai_tools`, `dacore_installations`, `dacore_modules`, `dacore_plugin_logs`, `dacore_settings`, `{prefix}users_rights*`
- Build your own admin HTML shell
- Use `#DACore:AuthTest@check!` as a permission guard — **it ignores the rights you pass**
- Register menu / rights / AI tools on every request (do it in **your** `Installation.php`)
- Use `$_SESSION` / `session_start()` — **MUST** `DSM::use('Shop')` (`AIRULES/20`)
- Use `install.php` on **your** module that works under DACore — use **`dainstall.php`** + `init/` copies (`AIRULES/35-DACORE-INSTALL.md` §4–§6). Do not blank root init files unless the user asked to export. **Never** apply `dainstall.php` / `init/` / inert stubs to `app/modules/DACore/` itself.

## Call map

```php
DotApp::call("DACore:Menu@register", $menuid, $data);            // bool
DotApp::call("DACore:Rights@createGroup!", $name, $creator);      // int|null
DotApp::call("DACore:Rights@createRight!", $groupId, $name, $desc, $module, $rightname, $creator); // int|null
DotApp::call("DACore:AITools@register", $toolid, $data);          // bool
DotApp::call("DACore:Page@withMenu!", $title, $body, $header, $css, $js, $menuId); // string HTML
DotApp::call("DACore:Installations@exist!", $module, $version);    // bool
DotApp::call("DACore:Installations@insert!", $module, $version, $status, $statusTxt);
```

Check every return value: `bool` helpers never throw and never log.

## Admin route pattern

```php
Router::get(Config::module("DACore", "prefixUrl") . "/shop-admin/items", "Shop:Admin@items!")
    ->before(function ($request) {
        return DotApp::call("#Shop:Rights@check!", $request, ['dotapp.root', 'Shop.items.view']);
    });
```

Permissions are `"{module}.{rightname}"`. Always include `dotapp.root`.

## Page rendering

Render your content with `Renderer` (`renderLayout()` + `setLayoutVar`), then pass the HTML to `Page@withMenu!`. The shell already loads `dotapp.js`, dotgrid, colors.css, core.css, modals and Notiflix — do not re-add them.

Prefer DACore widgets (cards, `btn`, dotgrid, Remix, Notiflix). **MUST search first:** grep `app/modules/DACore/` (read-only) and your module assets before writing a new library — the base already has many subpages and widgets. If it exists, use it; do not fork. **MUST** add CSS/JS in **your** module only when the search finds no equivalent (charts, ported controls). Pass them as `$css` / `$js` on `withMenu`. Classes `{lowercase_modulename}_*` (e.g. `.shop_chart`). Match admin colors from the loaded palette — never patch `app/modules/DACore/`.

Admin runtime is **`$dotapp`** (already in the shell). jQuery may coexist for **UI widgets only**. **All HTTP to the app** uses `$dotapp().form` / `$dotapp().load` / `dotbridge` — never `$.ajax` / `$.post` / raw `fetch` to DotApp endpoints. When porting jQuery plugins, **ask**, then **rewrite** as `$dotapp().fn(...)` (do not wrap `$.fn`). Playbook: `AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §4.C and `AIRULES/examples/EX-15-dotapp-js-library.md`. If DACore already ships the widget, use it — never copy DACore JS into your module.

Growing lists (logs, users, items) **MUST** use `paginate()` and an **interactive AJAX** pager on **first ship** (`DACore:Page@paginate!` `$callable` as buttons + `$dotapp().load()`). **MUST NOT** dump `->all()`, skip because “few rows now”, or `<a href="?page=">` / `location.reload()`. See `AIRULES/09` §3 and `AIRULES/33` §3.

**Persist:** PHP **MUST** re-check (2FA, rights, validation). A 2FA overlay covering Save is UX only — removing it **MUST** still fail on the server (`AIRULES/08`, `AIRULES/32` §6).

**Files:** `$dotapp().uploadFile` + `$request->upload()`. **MUST NOT** `FormData` + `load()` / `<fo-rm>`. PHP **MUST** reject `.php` / executables (extension + `finfo` MIME + headers); FE `accept=` is UX only.

## UI

`<dot-grid>` / `<dot-col any="12" md="6" ldesktop="6">` (`md` does not cascade). Icons: `ri ri-*`. Forms: `<fo-rm>` + `{{ formName(handler) }}` **MUST between** `<fo-rm>` and `</fo-rm>` — **only** real multi-field submit. Row actions / drag-and-drop = `$dotapp().load()` + encrypted `data-*`, never one `<fo-rm>` per button. After save/toggle on the same page **MUST** patch `reply.html` + toast — no `location.reload()`. **MUST** overlay the form/list until the request ends (Notiflix preferred **or** your module preloaders; desktop **and** mobile). Growing lists **MUST** AJAX-paginate. Operators **MUST** keep 2FA on; dangerous actions **MUST** step-up 2FA (`AIRULES/32-DACORE-RIGHTS.md` §6) with `$dotapp().twoFactor` and **PHP must verify the code before persist** (overlay is not the gate). Deletes **MUST** use a graphical confirm (`Notiflix.Confirm` or `$dotapp().modal`) — never `alert()` / `window.confirm()`. User-visible strings **MUST** be product copy — never prompt-echo (`AIRULES/05-VIEWS-TEMPLATES-ASSETS.md` §8).

## AI tools

`rights` must be non-empty and **wildcard-free** (empty = hidden from everyone). Handler signature `($data, $aiobj)`, returns JSON with `result` + `message`. `controller` string ends with `!`. Write tools that change a live admin view **MUST** return `ui_events` (`name` = tool id). Page JS listens for `DACore.AI.UIEvent`, filters by name, AJAX-refreshes — **MUST NOT** `location.reload()`. Other screens ignore. No secrets in `payload`. See `AIRULES/34-DACORE-AI-TOOLS.md` §5.

Examples: `AIRULES/examples/EX-D01` … `EX-D04`.
